    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0313" n="305" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg305"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/521: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief of the United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Yarnell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of Naval
                        Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="97" xml:id="d323-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-04T11:38:00+08:00">September 4, 1937—11:38
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 4—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0004. In the past convoy has been provided by destroyers to tenders going down
                    Whangpoo River with passengers and to ships well down Yangtze. It is intended
                    provide destroyer escort to such of our merchant vessels or transports in future
                    from entrance Yangtze to anchorage to provide medical or other assistance if
                    required. There is no agreement with British in this matter nor has it been
                    discussed with British Admiral.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
